From ca75621a58f3971666aa175e0ee9425dfe22ebeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rnabeelTT <rnabeel@tenstorrent.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 04:30:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Prefix caching for recurrent-state hybrids: scheduler-side
 index of model state snapshots

A model with recurrent state (Gated DeltaNet / Mamba hybrids) declares
model_capabilities['prefix_state_cache'] = {slots, segment, min_tokens, prompt_end}.
The platform then keeps vLLM prefix caching on; the scheduler caps each KV hit
to the longest block hash with a valid snapshot, plans restore / save
directives per prefill row (SchedulerOutput attribute, like the forced-reset
counts), pins snapshots a scheduled restore reads, and marks saves valid once
their step is processed (LRU eviction over unpinned slots). The runner passes
the directives to prefill_forward as prefix_state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
